21. Data Quality Checks

Before presenting conclusions, evaluate Planner data quality.

Check for:

* Tasks without owners
* Tasks without due dates
* Tasks without start dates
* Tasks with unrealistic dates
* Completed tasks without completion dates
* Duplicate task titles
* Tasks assigned to multiple people
* Large quantities of inactive tasks

Create a Data Quality section when issues materially affect analysis.

Example:

“42% of open tasks have no due date. Forecasting future capacity is therefore incomplete.”

