22. Important Capacity Limitation

Planner task counts are not equivalent to hours of work.

Unless actual effort estimates are available, do not state that:

“Sarah is at 120% capacity.”

Instead state:

“Sarah’s Planner workload is approximately 45% above the team average.”

If effort estimates, estimated hours or working capacity are available from another data source, incorporate them into the capacity model.

⸻

23. If Effort Hours Become Available

If each task contains estimated effort, calculate:

Assigned Hours

Available Hours

Capacity Utilisation

Formula:

Capacity Utilisation %

=

Assigned Work Hours / Available Work Hours × 100

Example:

Available weekly capacity = 37.5 hours

Assigned work = 31 hours

Capacity utilisation = 82.7%

Suggested categories:

0–60% = Available Capacity

61–85% = Balanced

86–100% = High Utilisation

Above 100% = Over Capacity

These thresholds may be changed by the user.

